    "key_findings": [
      "Integrating technical indicators and news sentiment into a mean-variance optimization framework outperforms traditional baselines such as momentum strategy, equal-weighted portfolios, and Bitcoin long-short strategies in cumulative returns and Sharpe ratios.",
      "Combining sentiment information alongside technical indicators produces more consistent performance gains than relying on sentiment-only or technical-only strategies.",
      "All strategies experience severe drawdowns during market-wide stress periods such as the 2022 cryptocurrency downturn, demonstrating that current signals alone cannot fully protect the portfolio during extreme market shocks."
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "Strategies experience relatively large drawdowns during sharp market declines, indicating limited responsiveness to extreme fluctuations in volatile environments.",
      "The risk model relies on a 180-day rolling covariance without shrinkage or robust adjustments, making it sensitive to noise and large price swings.",
      "The model does not account for heavy-tailed return behavior, which may lead to underestimating extreme events."
    ],
